    "title": "Preview and Design modes land in the in-app browser",
    "intro": "Today's nightly is a single, substantial change: the browser panel gains dedicated Preview and Design modes, backed by a new CDP-driven element inspector that streams inspection results end-to-end from the Rust backend into the UI. Both shipped server channels now enable the Chromium/CDP backend by default so this works in web-server builds as well as the desktop packages for Linux, macOS, and Windows.",
