        "title": "Preview and Design modes for the in-app browser",
        "summary": "The browser panel now offers explicit Preview and Design modes, including a design toolbar, an element inspector, and a full CDP inspection pipeline from Chromium through the server into the UI.",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Added Preview and Design modes to the browser panel, with a new BrowserDesignToolbar and BrowserDesignInspector plus shared design-mode and design-context modules driving how the viewport, tabs, and browser instance behave in each mode.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Implemented a CDP-backed element inspector: a new inspect module and Inspect client message flow inspection requests through the browser session loop and stream InspectionResult events over the WebSocket handler as 'inspection' payloads to the interface.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Enabled the Chromium/CDP browser backend by default on both dev-channel and stable-channel server builds so Preview and Design work in web-server deployments as well as the desktop package, while feature-minimal builds can still fall back to the stub backend.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "high"
          },
          {
            "text": "Extended the agent chat panel, browser API client, and browser-panel store to carry design-mode context, and expanded CDP smoke tests and browser viewport tests to cover the new inspection and mode-switching behavior.",
            "commit_shas": [
              "fe5f7b0be4b01ffe678272ec42ce74463d8e53a3"
            ],
            "confidence": "medium"
          }
